          "title": "You'll want to know: ख़ेमा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ख़ेमा — khemā — \"a tent (for camping)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नदी के किनारे हमारा ख़ेमा था। nadī ke kināre hamārā khemā thā. Our tent was on the river bank."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ख़ेमा (khemā) is usually traced to Arabic khayma, \"a tent\", which came through Persian; the diphthong has become a plain e."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
